# Line endings that are part of the CONTRACT, not a preference.
#
# Two files here are consumed by Linux tooling and by byte-exact comparison, so
# core.autocrlf turning them into CRLF on a Windows checkout is a real failure
# rather than a cosmetic one:
#
#   tests/golden-dump.sha256  is compared line-for-line against a manifest
#       generated inside a Linux container. A trailing \r on every line made all
#       2,452 entries differ and looked precisely like a catastrophic decoder
#       divergence. It was the file's line endings.
#
#   tests/*.sh  runs under bash in that container. CRLF makes bash fail with
#       "\r: command not found", or worse, silently mis-parse.

* text=auto

tests/golden-dump.sha256   text eol=lf
*.sh                       text eol=lf

#   .github/workflows/*.yml  run: blocks execute under bash on the runners. CRLF
#       there produces "\r: command not found" exactly as it does in a .sh file,
#       and the failure surfaces as a broken CI job rather than anything that
#       points at line endings.
*.yml                      text eol=lf
*.yaml                     text eol=lf

# Binary assets: never touched, never diffed as text.
*.zip    binary
*.ico    binary
*.png    binary
*.wav    binary

# These authoring records include byte hashes of prompts, scripts and reports.
# Preserve their recorded bytes across checkout platforms, including line endings.
art/cartoon/walk-pilot/** -text whitespace=cr-at-eol

# This hashed historical capture manifest includes a final blank line.
art/cartoon/walk-pilot/directional-cycle-v1/review-evidence/direction-clearance-manifest-v1.json whitespace=cr-at-eol,-blank-at-eof
